  "id": "corbettmansions",
  "note": "CORBETT MANSIONS: twelve storeys of interwar red-brick mansion flats on Lever Lane, beside Watts The Damage, with Mixed Bag Variety Store in the ground floor (docs/proposals/marrow-midrises.md).\n\nA block built to look like a bank, and shaped like one too: a two-storey stone plinth, a brick shaft banded in stone, then two setbacks with a stone cornice under each, and an attic carrying the timber water tank. A bay of wide windows runs up the middle of the front past the first setback, and a stair tower runs up the back. It stops at twelve so the Meridian, two tiles away, stays the tower.\n\n⚠ THE NAME IS THE BIGGEST LETTERING ON THE FRONT, AND IT IS ABOVE THE SHOP'S. CORBETT MANSIONS is cut across the whole stone frieze at the top of the plinth; MIXED BAG and VARIETY STORE are boards on the shopfront below it, over the awning. Two names on one front, and different businesses, so it is allowed.\n\n⚠ EVERY MASS IS A SQUARE. F() rotates a box's position to the entrance and leaves its footprint pointing north, so the bay and the stair tower are square boxes off centre, and the setbacks are centred squares. Nothing here can turn out from under itself at another facing.\n\n⚠ THE BRICK IS IN BRICK_WALL, so the wall draws no window grid, and every window is authored, one repeat per column with one row per storey.",
  "pal": "ty_corbett",
